course: dictionary
lesson: 2112
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «He is controlling the drone» means he is in charge of it and making it do what he wants.
explain: A controlling person is different. They try too hard to control other people and what they do, which is unkind and unfair. The same word can be fine in one sentence and a problem in another, so read the clues around it.
explain: Look at this sentence: «A tired brain is worse at controlling temper, so players short of sleep argue more and get booked more easily.» Here controlling means keeping your temper in check. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Controlling means being in charge of something or making it do what you want.
fact: A controlling person tries too hard to control other people and what they do, which is unkind and unfair.
fact: «Controlling temper» means keeping your temper under control.
fact: In science, you learn about controlling variables in a fair test.
fact: A controlling friend or partner who tells you who to see or checks your phone is a warning sign: tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «He is controlling the drone.» What does controlling mean here? | *Making it do what he wants, being in charge of it | Crashing it into a tree | Watching it from far away | Painting it red
exercise: What is a controlling person? | A friend who is always cheerful | A person who can swim very fast | A person who likes to draw | *A person who tries too hard to control other people
exercise: In science, controlling variables means | *Keeping everything the same except the one thing you are testing | Making the test go faster | Changing everything at once | Forgetting to write the results down
test: Which word is the -ing form of control? | controlled | control | *controlling | controls
test: «A controlling share means enough to have power over a company.» What does a controlling share give you? | *Power over a company | A new office chair | A free lunch | Nothing at all
exam: According to «A tired brain is worse at controlling temper», why do tired players get booked more easily? | *They argue more, because a tired brain is worse at controlling temper | They are too happy to play | They run faster than everyone else
